# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: knot-permute-typed-wrappers
why: knot_aead_absorb_data/encrypt/decrypt call their permutation through a knot_permute_t (void (*)(void *, uint8_t)),
why: but the pointers are cast from knot256_permute_6/knot384_permute_7/knot512_permute_7, which take a typed state
why: pointer (UBSan -fsanitize=function: call through pointer to incorrect function type, knot-aead.c:110/130/157;
why: a trap on WebAssembly). The patch adds wrappers with the exact knot_permute_t signature that forward to the real
why: permutation (void* converts implicitly to the state pointer) and passes them instead of the casted functions.
why: The same permutation is called with the same state and rounds, so output is unchanged.
file: upstream/knot-aead.c
count: 1
find: aead_cipher_t const knot_aead_128_256_cipher = {
replace: static void ns_knot256_permute_6(void *state, uint8_t rounds) { knot256_permute_6(state, rounds); } static void ns_knot384_permute_7(void *state, uint8_t rounds) { knot384_permute_7(state, rounds); } static void ns_knot512_permute_7(void *state, uint8_t rounds) { knot512_permute_7(state, rounds); } aead_cipher_t const knot_aead_128_256_cipher = {
patch: knot-permute-use-wrapper-256
why: pass the correctly typed wrapper instead of a cast function pointer (see knot-permute-typed-wrappers).
file: upstream/knot-aead.c
count: 4
find: (knot_permute_t)knot256_permute_6,
replace: ns_knot256_permute_6,
